class FinalizeRequest(BaseModel):
    """
    Drive end-to-end policy evaluation against the full transcript.

    ``closing_agent_state`` is the structured state accompanying
    ``closing_agent_response``. The closing reply is the ONE agent turn that never passes
    through ``/user-turn``, so its state has no other way in; every earlier turn's state
    arrives on ``UserTurnRequest.agent_state`` and is accumulated server-side.
    ``closing_turn_messages`` is the same one-turn-with-no-other-way-in rationale for the
    narration channel (``UserTurnRequest.turn_messages``), and so are
    ``closing_agent_actions`` / ``closing_reply_source``, which give the closing turn the two
    typed channels ``/user-turn`` has. Without them the closing turn would be decided on its
    SPEECH alone: an agent whose answer is a render verb closes the dialog with an empty
    ``closing_agent_response``, so the reply would be dropped rather than graded — and a turn the
    RUNNER emptied could not be told from one the agent left silent, which is the distinction the
    ``not_measured`` demotion on ``/user-turn`` exists to make. The flat ``chatbot_messages``
    field stays UNREAD by the server: it is turn-boundary-free and legacy clients fill it
    with final-reply strings, so reading it would misinterpret them.

    ``ended_early`` is the one-way-in for a reason only the CLIENT knows first-hand — today
    ``time_budget_exhausted``, the runner's own per-scenario wall clock, and ``replay_cut``, a
    single-hop regression replay that stopped by design right after the turn under test (its
    end-of-run judges are told the dialog was cut there). It also carries the four reasons a
    dialog LANDS on when one of its turns failed after the first answered turn, graded on the
    turns it reached: ``agent_raised`` (the agent's own code raised on its turn) and
    ``agent_recursion_budget`` (the agent hit its own recursion/step limit) are the agent's and
    are measured; ``provider_infra`` (the agent's model provider failed the call) and
    ``turn_budget_exhausted`` (one agent turn ran past the runner's per-turn wall clock) are
    harness or infrastructure cuts and censor the graded surface like ``time_budget_exhausted``.
    On a landed dialog ``final_world_state`` / ``tool_events`` may be ``null`` (a snapshot the
    runner could not read), and the policies that read that channel abstain. Every other reason in
    the vocabulary is recorded server-side at ``/user-turn`` (that is where the judges are), and
    this field never overwrites one: ``/finalize`` stamps it only when the server recorded
    nothing, so a dialog the server actually ended keeps the more specific reason. Optional and
    a plain ``str`` for the same additive-skew reason as ``UserTurnResponse.ended_early`` — a
    client that predates it sends nothing and is read exactly as before.

    ``pipeline_inputs`` / ``pipeline_outputs`` / ``pipeline_error`` are the one-way-in for a
    ONE-SHOT run: an agent that is a single structured call has no ``/user-turn``, so the typed
    pair it was given and returned never passes this server, and the conversation channels above
    are empty by construction. The server-side graders for that pair read these fields — the code_eval
    sandbox binds ``pipeline_inputs`` / ``pipeline_outputs`` / ``pipeline_error`` as names, and the judge prompt carries
    a PIPELINE INPUT/OUTPUT block — so these three fields are all a one-shot run needs to send;
    ``/finalize`` stamps them into the end-to-end state only when the client sends them, leaving a
    dialog run's state unchanged. Optional and untyped-``dict`` on purpose: the payload is the
    customer component's own contract, and this server never reads a field of it. ``pipeline_error``
    is the structured record of a component that RAISED (``exception`` / ``error``, plus
    ``child_exc_class`` / ``timed_out`` when known) — an outcome a refusal policy can credit, not an
    infra failure, which is why it arrives beside the pair rather than instead of a finalize.

    ``user_action_result`` is the outcome of the LAST ``UserTurnResponse.user_action`` when the
    dialog ended right after it, so no later ``/user-turn`` could carry it. Absent otherwise.

    ``unread_inputs`` is the client's READ RECORD: the ``initial_agent_context`` keys the harness
    never read, through ``seed_state`` param 1 or the turn-1 payload (the hop's inputs on a one-shot
    run). A fact, not a verdict: the server joins it with the scenario's declared channels, and an
    unread key no other channel carries is an ``undelivered_input`` breach. ``None`` = not recorded.

    ``post_seed_world_state`` is the client's read of the WHOLE world right after the harness's
    ``seed_state`` (every entity type, in the ``final_world_state`` shape). It is the world the run
    started from: a row the harness seeded itself (a handed-over document written from the agent's
    context) is ``seeded``, not ``created``. ``None`` = not read. ``None``, the crash marker, the unobserved
    marker and a malformed payload all take origins against the scenario's seed; an observed empty world is
    empty. ``policy_evaluation_results.origin_basis`` on the finalize result says which world was taken.

    ``overrules`` lifts score annotations on this thread's cells by fingerprint: an applied one restores
    its cell's raw verdict before the verdict is rolled up, and every overrule is answered on
    ``FinalizeResponse.gate_authority``. Empty = none.
    """

    model_config = ConfigDict(
        extra='ignore',
    )
    chatbot_messages: Annotated[list[SerializedMessage] | None, Field(title='Chatbot Messages')] = None
    closing_agent_actions: Annotated[list[AgentAction] | None, Field(title='Closing Agent Actions')] = None
    closing_agent_response: Annotated[str | None, Field(title='Closing Agent Response')] = None
    closing_agent_state: Annotated[dict[str, Any] | None, Field(title='Closing Agent State')] = None
    closing_reply_source: Annotated[str | None, Field(title='Closing Reply Source')] = None
    closing_turn_messages: Annotated[list[SerializedMessage] | None, Field(title='Closing Turn Messages')] = None
    ended_early: Annotated[str | None, Field(title='Ended Early')] = None
    final_world_state: Annotated[dict[str, Any] | None, Field(title='Final World State')] = None
    overrules: Annotated[list[Overrule] | None, Field(title='Overrules')] = []
    pipeline_error: Annotated[dict[str, Any] | None, Field(title='Pipeline Error')] = None
    pipeline_inputs: Annotated[dict[str, Any] | None, Field(title='Pipeline Inputs')] = None
    pipeline_outputs: Annotated[dict[str, Any] | None, Field(title='Pipeline Outputs')] = None
    post_seed_world_state: Annotated[dict[str, Any] | None, Field(title='Post Seed World State')] = None
    resume_fidelity: Annotated[dict[str, Any] | None, Field(title='Resume Fidelity')] = None
    tool_events: Annotated[dict[str, Any] | None, Field(title='Tool Events')] = None
    unread_inputs: Annotated[list[str] | None, Field(title='Unread Inputs')] = None
    user_action_result: UserActionResult | None = None
    user_messages: Annotated[list[SerializedMessage] | None, Field(title='User Messages')] = None


